v1.3.0-2: Purple Team tool expansion Phase 8C+8D — enrichment + dormant post-exploit

Hypothesis enrichment (Phase 8C):
- OSV (api.osv.dev, keyless): aliases, severity, affected packages —
  bounded, cached a day, audited like every lookup
- GitHub Advisory Database (api.github.com/advisories, keyless): GHSA id,
  severity, patched versions
- CWE ids extracted from the NVD record's weaknesses list (copilot/cve.py)
  -> enrichment["cwes"]
- nuclei_meta.py baked script: scans the image's /opt/nuclei-templates
  front-matter for the CVE/term; a template match is another
  exploit-availability signal (sandbox-local, no egress), spawned from
  enrich_hypotheses exactly like searchsploit
- report.jinja renders OSV/GHSA/CWE/nuclei rows in the known-risk block;
  _normalize_enrichment keeps StrictUndefined safe

Post-exploit (Phase 8D, DORMANT by design):
- impacket-scripts in the image; read-only recon tools allowlisted
  (GetNPUsers/GetUserSPNs/GetADUsers/findDelegation, -dc-ip {target}
  first, context as {term}) — secretsdump/atexec/wmiexec/psexec and all
  credential-extraction/execution tools stay OFF the list entirely
  (tested)
- bloodhound-python allowlist template (--collection All, {term} domain,
  {target} dc-ip) — it was already in the image; the entrypoint sync now
  covers it
- cloud_meta.py baked script: probes AWS/GCP/Azure/Aliyun metadata
  endpoints from inside the sandbox, response capped at 2000 chars;
  inert by design (nothing reachable from gVisor — the absence is the
  evidence). Added to the fixed POST_EXPLOIT_PLAN
- POST_EXPLOIT_DORMANT_TOOLS set documents the impacket/bloodhound
  status; plan-coverage test excludes it, a second test pins the dormant
  tools OUT of the plan

Tests: 530 -> 549.

